{"author":"Joe Oakhart","author_email":"joeoakhart@navapbc.com","data":{"alias":"unequal-godsent-fox","creation_channel":"cli","description":"Discovered from ADEVX-102.\n\nA ticket that declares a resolvable base branch now causes two git ls-remote calls for the same repo and branch in one start. The first runs in _start through IntakeContext.base_resolver.resolve_base, which uses only the truthiness of the result and discards the SHA. The second runs inside TemporalStarter.start through remote_head.\n\nCarrying the resolved SHA from the pre-check into IntakeStart would remove the second lookup. The reviewer rated the performance impact at zero, so this is tidiness rather than a hot path.\n\nFiles: services/orchestration/intake_reconciler.py, services/orchestration/intake_runtime.py.","id":"862d-a880-a31f-4766","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["adevx","follow-on","intake"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Reuse the resolved base SHA instead of running git ls-remote twice"},"env_id":"8c3ef925-fbdc-4d88-8d59-f391cf59568c","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1789496992593205001,"uuid":"2c49807c-5405-4c4f-a803-e6c290e9ab12"}